WEBVTT

00:01.501 --> 00:03.920
-[people chattering]
-[bell tolls in distance]

00:10.635 --> 00:12.595
-[laughter]
-[bell continues tolling]

00:14.014 --> 00:16.016
[people clamoring]

00:16.349 --> 00:17.726
[resident 1] This way! Hurry!

00:17.809 --> 00:19.811
[wind blowing]

00:22.439 --> 00:23.690
-[resident 2] Over here!
-[laughter]

00:23.773 --> 00:25.316
-[ground rumbling]
-[residents exclaim]

00:27.110 --> 00:29.279
[crowd murmuring]

00:29.362 --> 00:30.697
-[resident 3] What's going on?
-[resident 4] Are you all right?

00:30.780 --> 00:31.781
[resident 3 exclaims]

00:31.865 --> 00:34.284
[crowd murmuring]

00:34.367 --> 00:36.661
[ground continues rumbling]

00:48.256 --> 00:50.008
-[building cracking]
-[crowd screaming]

00:53.053 --> 00:55.472
Nagan Labyrinth City

00:55.555 --> 00:58.058
[narrator]
<i>This is the story of the first one.</i>

00:58.558 --> 01:02.479
Episode 1
Soujirou the Willow-Sword

01:03.063 --> 01:06.191
<i>But for Yuno the Distant Talon,</i>

01:06.274 --> 01:10.236
<i>it begins with a memory,</i>
<i>of a school friend named Lucelles.</i>

01:11.196 --> 01:12.280
Minia
Yuno the Distant Talon

01:12.363 --> 01:13.490
Huh?

01:17.494 --> 01:18.787
[gasps in awe]

01:25.126 --> 01:26.127
[professor] Word Arts

01:26.211 --> 01:30.048
is the general term for techniques
that distort various natural phenomena,

01:30.131 --> 01:32.467
using the will embedded in words.

01:32.550 --> 01:36.763
Irrespective of the speaker's race
or linguistic system.

01:37.347 --> 01:40.767
Word Arts can only be used in this world.

01:40.850 --> 01:42.018
It doesn't work the same…

01:42.102 --> 01:44.521
-[gasps]
-…in the world of the so-called visitors.

01:45.772 --> 01:46.773
[Lucelles] Yuno!

01:47.357 --> 01:48.775
-[gasps]
-[giggles]

01:48.858 --> 01:50.235
Are you busy today?

01:50.819 --> 01:53.238
W… Well, not really.

01:53.571 --> 01:54.614
How come?

01:54.697 --> 01:57.075
Can you teach me Force Arts?

01:57.158 --> 01:58.201
Huh?

01:58.284 --> 01:59.327
Me?

01:59.410 --> 02:01.496
[Lucelles] Yep, you're great at it, Yuno.

02:01.579 --> 02:05.333
It's better than my other arts, but…

02:05.416 --> 02:06.835
[Lucelles] I'm counting on you, then.

02:06.918 --> 02:08.211
Okay?

02:09.045 --> 02:10.755
O-Okay.

02:11.798 --> 02:14.801
[Yuno] <i>We lived in Nagan Labyrinth City,</i>
<i>a town of scholars and explorers,</i>

02:15.301 --> 02:19.597
<i>that was built from the center</i>
<i>of the Great Labyrinth of Kiyazuna,</i>

02:19.681 --> 02:23.017
<i>the self-proclaimed Demon King.</i>

02:23.101 --> 02:24.602
[metal clanging]

02:24.686 --> 02:25.895
-[bangs]
-[grunts]

02:26.604 --> 02:28.523
[swordsmen clamoring]

02:28.606 --> 02:29.732
[shouts]

02:32.026 --> 02:33.736
[powering down]

02:33.820 --> 02:34.988
[thuds]

02:35.738 --> 02:36.781
[swordsman 1] We got it!

02:36.865 --> 02:39.242
[swordsman 2] I can't believe
it came out from the Great Labyrinth.

02:39.826 --> 02:42.036
[swordsman 3]
It probably went in after a bandit.

02:42.120 --> 02:43.121
[swordsmen gasp]

02:43.204 --> 02:44.664
[swordsman 4] It's on the move again!

02:44.747 --> 02:46.833
[swordsman 5] The seal!
Find its life seal!

02:47.584 --> 02:49.169
[metal clanking in distance]

02:51.421 --> 02:52.922
Like this?

02:53.923 --> 02:55.842
From Lucelles to the stone of Nagan.

02:55.925 --> 02:57.844
Scales of the sky.
Waves of red grain. Dance.

02:59.429 --> 03:01.055
[stone ringing]

03:03.433 --> 03:05.351
-[chuckles]
-You're great at this!

03:06.102 --> 03:07.729
[Lucelles] That's poisonous, you know?

03:07.812 --> 03:08.980
What?

03:09.564 --> 03:11.065
[Lucelles] That's why the Central Kingdom

03:11.149 --> 03:13.902
crowned Sephite
of the United Western Kingdom as Queen

03:13.985 --> 03:15.361
and created Aureatia.

03:16.529 --> 03:17.697
Is that so?

03:18.489 --> 03:20.283
[Lucelles]
Yuno, do you have a crush on anyone?

03:20.366 --> 03:21.659
[Yuno] What?

03:22.493 --> 03:23.494
Uh…

03:24.287 --> 03:25.663
[Lucelles] They say the Great Labyrinth…

03:28.249 --> 03:32.045
must have so many secrets and relics,
that we could never fully unearth it all,

03:32.128 --> 03:34.130
even when we become adults.

03:34.631 --> 03:35.632
[Yuno] Right.

03:35.715 --> 03:38.384
[Lucelles] No matter who you are
or what your past is,

03:38.760 --> 03:41.304
the path to glory is open to everyone.

03:42.555 --> 03:43.556
[giggles]

03:44.849 --> 03:45.892
[Yuno gasps]

03:50.063 --> 03:52.774
[Yuno] <i>There's no need</i>
<i>to be scared of anything anymore.</i>

03:52.857 --> 03:54.442
<i>The True Demon King is dead.</i>

03:55.276 --> 03:56.945
<i>The age of fear is over.</i>

03:57.862 --> 04:02.033
<i>Now, the two of us</i>
<i>can dream of a future filled with glory.</i>

04:03.534 --> 04:05.536
[chatter and laughter]

04:06.871 --> 04:08.873
-[ground rumbling]
-[all screaming]

04:09.874 --> 04:12.043
[structure cracking]

04:12.126 --> 04:13.211
[gasps]

04:14.212 --> 04:16.214
-[structure cracking]
-[yelps]

04:22.637 --> 04:24.138
[both gasping]

04:24.222 --> 04:26.224
[disembodied voices]

04:28.101 --> 04:31.562
-[both gasping]
-[object whirring]

04:32.188 --> 04:34.649
[Yuno] <i>But this was that future.</i>

04:35.733 --> 04:37.193
[coughing]

04:38.069 --> 04:39.988
[Lucelles groans]

04:40.613 --> 04:42.365
[Lucelles whimpers]

04:43.074 --> 04:44.367
[Yuno sobbing]
Lucelles…

04:45.201 --> 04:46.202
Lucelles!

04:46.286 --> 04:48.621
[Lucelles shrieking in agony]

04:51.916 --> 04:54.002
[shrieking continues]

04:54.919 --> 04:56.087
[blood splattering]

04:57.088 --> 04:58.298
[Yuno] No…

04:58.589 --> 05:00.425
Stop!

05:02.677 --> 05:03.678
[gasps]

05:04.470 --> 05:06.931
[Yuno screaming]

05:09.142 --> 05:11.352
[panting]

05:12.270 --> 05:13.354
[resident] P… Please help--

05:13.438 --> 05:14.439
[loud thud]

05:17.150 --> 05:18.151
[Yuno grunts]

05:18.234 --> 05:20.236
[♪ foreboding music playing]

05:20.320 --> 05:21.321
[Yuno gasps]

05:21.821 --> 05:22.822
No…

05:23.448 --> 05:25.408
[Yuno screams]
No!

05:26.576 --> 05:29.120
[Yuno breathing heavily]

05:38.796 --> 05:40.131
…died too.

05:41.132 --> 05:42.467
I should have…

05:43.092 --> 05:44.635
died too.

05:46.012 --> 05:47.972
[Yuno] <i>Nobody understood.</i>

05:48.639 --> 05:50.433
<i>Nobody understood anything.</i>

05:51.601 --> 05:53.728
<i>Even though the True Demon King had died,</i>

05:54.479 --> 05:56.147
<i>it wasn't the end.</i>

05:56.731 --> 05:58.900
[Yuno sobbing]
No! Make it stop!

05:58.983 --> 06:00.985
-[footsteps approaching]
-[gasps]

06:05.114 --> 06:07.033
[Yuno] From Yuno
to the Arrowhead of Fipike.

06:07.116 --> 06:08.618
Index finger axis. Lattice star.

06:08.701 --> 06:10.703
Exploding sparks. Spin!

06:17.627 --> 06:18.669
[thuds]

06:18.753 --> 06:19.962
Huh?

06:20.630 --> 06:21.631
[Yuno] Why?

06:22.256 --> 06:24.258
Why did you die just from that?

06:24.342 --> 06:26.135
That means Lucelles…

06:26.761 --> 06:28.471
could have been saved!

06:30.515 --> 06:32.850
[in strained voice]
I could have saved her…

06:32.934 --> 06:34.644
-[approaching footsteps]
-[gasps]

06:37.105 --> 06:39.524
From Yuno to the Arrowhead of Fipike.

06:39.607 --> 06:42.110
Index finger axis. Lattice star.
Exploding sparks. Spin!

06:43.694 --> 06:46.155
-[thuds]
-[Yuno trembling]

06:46.239 --> 06:49.117
Go ahead and kill me…

06:49.200 --> 06:50.284
Go on.

06:50.368 --> 06:52.703
You'll kill me
no matter what I say, right?

06:52.787 --> 06:56.165
Fine by me! I want to die!

06:56.249 --> 06:58.000
That's right! I--

06:58.084 --> 06:59.544
[metallic ringing]

07:01.671 --> 07:02.839
[metallic ringing]

07:05.383 --> 07:07.927
[crashing]

07:12.223 --> 07:13.224
Huh?

07:13.307 --> 07:14.600
Yo.

07:14.684 --> 07:16.144
[Yuno whimpers]

07:16.227 --> 07:17.228
[gasps]

07:17.311 --> 07:19.939
So you like dying, huh?

07:20.898 --> 07:22.108
-Well?
-[gasps]

07:22.692 --> 07:25.111
I'm asking if you like dying.

07:25.194 --> 07:27.488
[Yuno trembling]
Yes… I mean no.

07:27.572 --> 07:29.490
What's up with you?

07:29.574 --> 07:30.825
You're going to miss out.

07:31.451 --> 07:33.828
Things are about to get fun for humans.

07:33.911 --> 07:35.746
F-Fun?

07:35.830 --> 07:39.125
Yup. Once everything else goes away.

07:39.625 --> 07:43.713
[visitor] You'll get to choose
where you go and what you do.

07:43.796 --> 07:45.047
Won't that be great?

07:45.965 --> 07:50.386
[Yuno] <i>You couldn't do something like this</i>
<i>with a chipped practice sword.</i>

07:51.304 --> 07:52.305
<i>Wait…</i>

07:52.388 --> 07:54.056
Are you a visitor?

07:54.140 --> 07:57.226
So, you call us that in this town, too?

07:57.560 --> 07:59.562
Well, call us what you like.

07:59.645 --> 08:01.147
It doesn't interest me.

08:01.772 --> 08:03.024
[Yuno gasps]

08:03.107 --> 08:04.484
Surely not…

08:04.567 --> 08:06.527
Did you defeat them all?

08:06.611 --> 08:09.322
[visitor] There are machines
in this world too, huh?

08:09.405 --> 08:11.824
What are they called again? Golems?

08:11.908 --> 08:14.827
No number of them can match my sword.

08:14.911 --> 08:16.412
[grunts]

08:16.496 --> 08:18.247
-[Yuno] No match for your sword?
-[gags]

08:18.331 --> 08:20.458
These leaves aren't edible!

08:20.917 --> 08:21.918
[Yuno] Yeah.

08:22.001 --> 08:23.961
Bundleroot grass is poisonous.

08:24.045 --> 08:25.338
[visitor] I thought so.

08:25.922 --> 08:28.424
Don't you have any food on you?

08:28.508 --> 08:32.345
[Yuno] You should run away from here.
You must!

08:32.428 --> 08:36.057
No matter how strong you are,
this place is doomed!

08:36.140 --> 08:39.435
Come on, don't get angry.
Why is it doomed?

08:39.519 --> 08:40.728
Why, you ask?

08:40.811 --> 08:42.355
[shouts]
Can't you see that?

08:42.939 --> 08:46.192
[Yuno] Can you kill that thing
with just one sword?

08:46.275 --> 08:48.277
[♪ tense music playing]

08:50.738 --> 08:52.406
The Great Labyrinth itself

08:52.907 --> 08:55.159
turned out to be one huge golem.

08:56.244 --> 08:59.747
It might be a monster created to defeat

08:59.830 --> 09:01.290
the True Demon King!

09:01.916 --> 09:03.042
[gasps]

09:03.125 --> 09:04.126
Heh.

09:06.045 --> 09:07.672
-[grunts]
-[crashing]

09:10.675 --> 09:11.676
[thuds]

09:12.718 --> 09:13.719
[trembling]

09:13.803 --> 09:15.680
[visitor] So you've got no food?

09:15.763 --> 09:18.516
I'm even fine with grass or bugs.
[grunts]

09:19.058 --> 09:21.227
I still haven't had breakfast.

09:21.310 --> 09:23.980
I… I have some travel ration.

09:24.438 --> 09:27.191
But it doesn't really taste of much.

09:27.275 --> 09:29.068
[visitor]
Talking to you is a bit of a pain.

09:29.652 --> 09:31.612
All right, give me some of that.

09:31.696 --> 09:33.197
Call it an exchange.

09:33.281 --> 09:34.365
[Yuno] An exchange?

09:34.448 --> 09:37.368
I'll take care of that
huge lump of metal for you.

09:37.743 --> 09:40.162
I was just getting around to it, actually.

09:40.705 --> 09:42.290
[visitor] This will be fun, huh?

09:42.373 --> 09:43.833
[Yuno trembling]

09:43.916 --> 09:45.209
[visitor] Very fun.

09:45.960 --> 09:49.463
[Yuno] W… Who the heck are you?

09:49.797 --> 09:53.050
[visitor] Soujirou Yagyuu,
of the Yagyuu Shinkage-ryu.

09:53.551 --> 09:56.971
I'm the last Yagyuu on Earth.

09:57.722 --> 09:59.682
[narrator] <i>A visitor
from the Distant World,</i>

10:00.016 --> 10:01.767
<i>much different from ours.</i>

10:02.768 --> 10:06.564
<i>That swordsman arrived</i>
<i>with the darkest of omens.</i>

10:07.064 --> 10:10.985
Ishura
Golem, Word Arts of Life

10:11.736 --> 10:14.905
[Soujirou] That move you did before,
it was Word Arts, right?

10:15.406 --> 10:17.283
-How do you do it?
-[Yuno] Huh?

10:17.366 --> 10:20.494
[Soujirou] You did it just now!
When you fired out that arrowhead.

10:21.078 --> 10:23.122
You can at least teach me that.

10:23.706 --> 10:27.126
I was taught
that visitors can't use this power.

10:27.835 --> 10:31.380
[Yuno] <i>"The Distant World of the visitors</i>
<i>is built solely on the laws of physics.</i>

10:32.006 --> 10:35.885
<i>They speak only using words of sound,</i>
<i>so it's beyond their understanding."</i>

10:35.968 --> 10:37.887
[Soujirou] <i>Words of sound?</i>

10:37.970 --> 10:39.847
<i>Oh, I see.</i>

10:39.930 --> 10:42.725
<i>It's not like you speak Japanese here.</i>

10:42.808 --> 10:46.020
[Yuno] <i>Word Arts is the reason</i>
<i>we can communicate right now.</i>

10:46.604 --> 10:49.607
<i>We use Word Arts to ask the air or objects</i>

10:49.690 --> 10:51.817
<i>to do things like move or burn.</i>

10:51.901 --> 10:54.278
[Soujirou groans]
I don't really get it, so whatever.

10:54.445 --> 10:55.738
Huh?

10:55.946 --> 10:57.531
A sword is much better.

10:57.615 --> 10:59.575
[gasps]
You'll die!

10:59.659 --> 11:00.660
[Soujirou] Doesn't matter.

11:00.743 --> 11:02.078
[gasps]

11:02.787 --> 11:04.163
[Yuno] Everyone is dead.

11:04.246 --> 11:06.040
Killing that thing now won't change that.

11:06.123 --> 11:08.000
Running away is the obvious thing to do!

11:08.626 --> 11:09.627
[Soujirou] Why's that?

11:10.294 --> 11:11.837
[hesitates]
Because…

11:13.798 --> 11:15.800
once you die it's all over.

11:16.300 --> 11:18.260
-All over, huh?
-[gasps]

11:18.344 --> 11:21.222
[Soujirou] So we give up just because
the enemy is an unbeatable monster?

11:21.806 --> 11:23.224
[Yuno] Well,

11:23.974 --> 11:25.351
what can I possibly do?

11:25.434 --> 11:28.145
Against that walking disaster?

11:28.229 --> 11:32.024
-I can't ask you to fight.
-[Soujirou] You're not involved in this.

11:32.108 --> 11:33.526
[Yuno gasps]

11:33.609 --> 11:35.319
I'm going to fight it
because it'll be fun.

11:36.195 --> 11:38.614
[Soujirou] There's no way it won't be fun.

11:38.698 --> 11:39.699
Just look.

11:40.032 --> 11:43.703
[golem growling]

11:43.786 --> 11:45.538
-[Soujirou] Time to do this.
-[Yuno] Huh…

11:45.621 --> 11:47.915
[♪ action music playing]

11:52.670 --> 11:53.713
[grunts]

11:57.425 --> 11:58.426
[Yuno gasping]

12:01.846 --> 12:03.264
[snickers]

12:07.810 --> 12:09.061
[gasps]

12:09.562 --> 12:10.646
[Yuno] How?

12:10.938 --> 12:11.981
How is he so fast?

12:16.402 --> 12:17.403
[exclaims]

12:23.993 --> 12:25.870
[Yuno groans]

12:30.833 --> 12:32.710
[breathes shakily, gasps]

12:32.793 --> 12:34.837
[♪ action music continues playing]

12:40.217 --> 12:41.260
[blasting]

12:51.604 --> 12:52.646
[snickering]

13:04.658 --> 13:05.659
[chuckles]

13:10.664 --> 13:11.957
[grunts]

13:14.210 --> 13:15.252
[clanks]

13:20.800 --> 13:22.802
[explosion]

13:24.720 --> 13:26.847
[golem]
From Nagan to the heart of Naganeruya.

13:26.931 --> 13:29.183
Flow of angular clouds.

13:29.266 --> 13:32.353
Edge of heaven and earth.

13:33.646 --> 13:36.607
Overflowing vast ocean.

13:41.487 --> 13:43.614
[humming]

13:45.407 --> 13:46.408
[Yuno] There it is.

13:47.368 --> 13:49.620
The light that scorched the city.

13:51.121 --> 13:52.790
[Yuno] That monster…

13:53.415 --> 13:55.459
can even use Thermal Arts.

13:57.086 --> 13:58.712
[golem] Burn.

13:58.796 --> 14:00.130
[silence]

14:00.214 --> 14:01.799
[rumbling]

14:03.050 --> 14:04.552
[explosion]

14:21.110 --> 14:23.028
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

14:25.906 --> 14:26.907
-[shouts]
-[sword clanks]

14:26.991 --> 14:28.367
[gasps]

14:31.495 --> 14:33.247
[powering down]

14:34.415 --> 14:36.792
[♪ tense music playing]

14:36.876 --> 14:38.544
[metal crashing]

14:42.965 --> 14:44.008
[gasps]

14:46.802 --> 14:47.845
[heavy thud]

14:48.679 --> 14:50.431
Thanks a lot.

14:50.514 --> 14:53.183
Those golems you chucked out
were the perfect footholds.

14:53.517 --> 14:55.060
My prediction was that

14:55.144 --> 14:57.897
it wouldn't harm itself
with its own Word Arts.

14:57.980 --> 15:00.357
[♪ grandiose music playing]

15:03.903 --> 15:06.030
-[Soujirou] I see.
-[metal scratching]

15:06.906 --> 15:08.365
For you…

15:11.160 --> 15:12.411
it all comes down

15:12.620 --> 15:14.079
to that.

15:14.163 --> 15:16.749
[♪ grandiose music continues]

15:16.832 --> 15:18.626
[narrator] <i>Eighth year of the Eiroku Era.</i>

15:18.959 --> 15:21.962
<i>Although it is</i>
<i>an anecdote of uncertain authenticity,</i>

15:22.379 --> 15:24.465
<i>the founder of Yagyuu Shinkage-ryu,</i>

15:24.548 --> 15:27.885
<i>Muneyoshi Yagyuu,</i>
<i>is said to have defeated a student</i>

15:27.968 --> 15:32.264
<i>of master swordsman Kamiizumi Nobutsuna,</i>
<i>with the Mutodori technique.</i>

15:32.765 --> 15:35.434
<i>Is it really possible to dodge</i>
<i>an opponent's attack,</i>

15:35.517 --> 15:38.938
<i>then steal their weapon</i>
<i>and use their own momentum</i>

15:39.980 --> 15:41.857
<i>to defeat them?</i>

15:42.566 --> 15:43.651
[sword clanging]

15:49.073 --> 15:50.282
<i>It is possible.</i>

15:50.366 --> 15:52.701
[♪ grandiose music rises]

15:52.785 --> 15:55.329
[Soujirou] I see it now. Your life seal.

15:58.457 --> 15:59.500
There it is!

16:01.418 --> 16:03.295
[sword ringing]

16:05.589 --> 16:07.132
I'll take that.

16:07.216 --> 16:08.926
Your weapon is mine now.

16:19.770 --> 16:20.896
[powering down]

16:27.695 --> 16:29.488
[wind rushing]

16:30.197 --> 16:32.199
And this is what they call Mutodori.

16:33.826 --> 16:35.619
[golem crashing]

16:41.625 --> 16:43.585
[powering down]

16:48.632 --> 16:50.718
[fire rumbling]

16:53.804 --> 16:55.931
[Yuno] <i>He really defeated it.</i>

16:56.932 --> 16:58.017
<i>But why?</i>

16:58.642 --> 17:00.936
<i>Why did the Great Labyrinth</i>
<i>start moving today?</i>

17:02.187 --> 17:04.023
<i>Don't tell me it's because of Soujirou.</i>

17:05.107 --> 17:07.693
<i>Did it react automatically</i>
<i>to his strength?</i>

17:08.569 --> 17:09.862
<i>Or…</i>

17:10.154 --> 17:11.947
<i>Did he activate it on purpose…</i>

17:12.656 --> 17:15.242
<i>because he wanted to fight it?</i>

17:18.245 --> 17:19.580
I cut it up!

17:20.164 --> 17:23.375
[Soujirou] It was more fun
than cutting up an M1.

17:23.459 --> 17:24.460
[Yuno] M1?

17:24.543 --> 17:28.464
[Soujirou] Yep, an M1 Abrams.
A tank. Understand?

17:28.756 --> 17:31.967
[scoffs]
Yeah, I thought not.

17:32.051 --> 17:33.969
The people here just don't get it.

17:34.344 --> 17:35.345
Why?

17:36.638 --> 17:37.848
[Yuno] How?

17:38.307 --> 17:40.309
[Soujirou]
If you imagine you created them,

17:40.392 --> 17:42.311
you can easily discover their life seal.

17:43.312 --> 17:45.355
[Soujirou] <i>Not their legs,</i>
<i>which are close to the ground.</i>

17:45.939 --> 17:47.983
<i>The waist carries too much bulk.</i>

17:48.067 --> 17:50.235
<i>The chest is a flame-throwing weapon.</i>

17:50.819 --> 17:53.489
<i>It struck first with its left arm.</i>

17:54.156 --> 17:56.575
<i>That just left the right arm.</i>

17:57.076 --> 17:58.368
[trembling breath]

17:58.452 --> 17:59.787
[Soujirou] All right, I'm off.

18:00.287 --> 18:01.288
W-Wait.

18:01.371 --> 18:02.456
Huh?

18:02.539 --> 18:04.541
Here. Travel ration for you…

18:04.917 --> 18:07.753
Oh, yeah! I was feeling hungry.
[chuckles]

18:07.836 --> 18:10.380
I had so much fun I completely forgot.

18:11.048 --> 18:12.424
Thanks.

18:13.592 --> 18:15.135
[gobbling]

18:15.886 --> 18:17.638
This tastes good!

18:17.721 --> 18:18.972
[chuckles]

18:19.056 --> 18:21.141
Better than bugs or grass.

18:21.225 --> 18:23.560
-Maybe this world isn't all that bad.
-[Yuno] <i>I see.</i>

18:23.644 --> 18:25.229
<i>I…</i>

18:25.562 --> 18:27.272
<i>hate strong people.</i>

18:28.398 --> 18:33.112
<i>Strong people</i>
<i>who made my life insignificant.</i>

18:33.570 --> 18:37.032
<i>Even once everything is destroyed,</i>
<i>and even tragedies are trampled over,</i>

18:37.616 --> 18:41.578
<i>a weakling like me</i>
<i>won't even have a right to deny that it.</i>

18:41.995 --> 18:45.582
<i>That's why,</i>
<i>even if it ends up being wrong,</i>

18:45.666 --> 18:48.377
<i>I have to support myself with something.</i>

18:48.794 --> 18:49.837
[slurping]

18:49.920 --> 18:52.172
All right, moving on.

18:52.256 --> 18:54.299
Time to find something even more fun.

18:54.383 --> 18:56.009
Which way should I go?

18:56.093 --> 18:57.427
-[Yuno] Aureatia.
-[Soujirou] Huh?

18:57.761 --> 18:59.054
[Yuno] You should go to Aureatia.

18:59.471 --> 19:01.932
It's become the largest country there is.

19:02.015 --> 19:03.183
Is that right?

19:03.267 --> 19:04.726
Are there some strong folks there?

19:05.310 --> 19:06.478
[Yuno] There are.

19:06.562 --> 19:07.938
[exclaims excitedly]

19:08.021 --> 19:11.191
The Council of Aureatia is gathering
heroes from around the world.

19:11.692 --> 19:14.945
[Yuno] They're planning
to do something big.

19:15.070 --> 19:16.613
[Soujirou chuckles]
Perfect.

19:17.197 --> 19:18.866
[Yuno] <i>There are people</i>
<i>who can kill this man.</i>

19:18.949 --> 19:21.160
<i>That's right, in this world,</i>

19:21.243 --> 19:23.287
<i>there are strong people who can do that.</i>

19:23.620 --> 19:28.125
<i>That's why, there are surely enemies</i>
<i>out there who won't lose even to you.</i>

19:28.792 --> 19:31.628
<i>There's the Second General of Aureatia,</i>
<i>who everybody knows the name of.</i>

19:32.254 --> 19:34.131
<i>Rosclay the Absolute.</i>

19:35.090 --> 19:37.134
<i>I know of Toroa the Awful,</i>

19:37.718 --> 19:39.720
<i>who hides away</i>
<i>in the distant Wyte Mountains.</i>

19:40.804 --> 19:44.641
<i>Krafnir the Hatch of Truth,</i>
<i>who speaks of mastering</i>

19:45.225 --> 19:47.144
<i>an unknown fifth system of Word Arts.</i>

19:48.103 --> 19:51.148
<i>There's the visitor who liberated</i>
<i>the Great Ice Fortress nine years ago,</i>

19:51.732 --> 19:54.151
<i>Kazuki the Black Tone.</i>

19:54.818 --> 19:57.070
<i>Or Lucnoca the Winter,</i>

19:58.530 --> 20:00.240
<i>who nobody has ever seen.</i>

20:01.241 --> 20:02.868
<i>In this world,</i>

20:02.951 --> 20:05.662
<i>countless threats and truths still remain.</i>

20:06.580 --> 20:09.166
<i>I have to know who this man is.</i>

20:09.666 --> 20:11.001
<i>I must find out,</i>

20:11.335 --> 20:12.920
<i>what exactly the Distant World is.</i>

20:14.004 --> 20:15.839
[Yuno] I'll guide you there.

20:16.131 --> 20:18.091
As a scholar of Nagan, that is.

20:18.175 --> 20:19.176
That way,

20:19.259 --> 20:21.803
Aureatia won't suspect us.

20:22.387 --> 20:24.556
Nice. I like that expression.

20:25.140 --> 20:27.559
-My expression?
-[Soujirou] Anyway, thanks for this.

20:28.185 --> 20:31.939
This means you can
do whatever you want from here on.

20:32.606 --> 20:33.690
You're free.

20:35.943 --> 20:38.904
Right. Thank you too.

20:42.199 --> 20:43.408
[Yuno] <i>I'm free…</i>

20:44.409 --> 20:46.411
<i>Now that I've lost everything,</i>

20:46.495 --> 20:49.331
<i>I feel like I can do something wild.</i>

20:49.915 --> 20:50.958
What's your name?

20:51.208 --> 20:52.209
Yuno.

20:53.710 --> 20:55.545
Yuno the Distant Talon.

20:56.213 --> 20:59.341
[narrator] <i>The horizon is crawling</i>
<i>with countless</i> shura.

20:59.925 --> 21:01.927
<i>This is the story of the first one.</i>

21:02.886 --> 21:05.430
<i>The one who can defeat </i>

21:05.514 --> 21:08.475
<i>numerous golems using only his sword.</i>

21:09.851 --> 21:13.188
<i>The one who exercises
supreme swordsmanship</i>

21:13.272 --> 21:15.899
<i>that reduces widespread legends</i>
<i>into mere truths.</i>

21:17.067 --> 21:20.404
<i>The one who understands
the vital spots of all living creatures,</i>

21:20.487 --> 21:23.073
<i>and possesses an instinct for slaughter.</i>

21:23.824 --> 21:27.160
<i>He couldn't even be contained</i>
<i>in the reality of his own world.</i>

21:27.244 --> 21:29.454
<i>He is the last swordsman.</i>

21:31.581 --> 21:36.420
<i>He is a Blade. He is a minia.
He is Soujirou the Willow-Sword.</i>

21:37.713 --> 21:39.715
[♪ theme music playing]

21:49.808 --> 21:52.811
ISHURA

23:07.677 --> 23:09.679
[fire rumbling]

23:14.059 --> 23:15.268
[Soujirou grunts]

23:16.311 --> 23:17.312
[sword clinks]

23:19.731 --> 23:20.774
[Yuno gasps]

23:24.361 --> 23:27.239
[Soujirou] Looks like someone was
only after their life seals.

23:27.322 --> 23:28.740
Heh.

23:29.324 --> 23:31.118
So there's another one out there.

23:31.201 --> 23:32.202
[muffled gasp]

23:34.079 --> 23:35.163
[snickers]

23:39.292 --> 23:40.836
Next: Episode 2
Alus the Star Runner

23:40.919 --> 23:41.920
Translated by Zacarias Hicks
